WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:12.589
"I'll come back to take you home at half-past five," Dr. Chilton said, leaving Pollyanna at Mr. Pendleton's door.

2
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:20.346
Pollyanna entered the great stone house and found Mr. Pendleton lying in bed as before.

3
00:00:20.347 --> 00:00:23.607
But this time he smiled when she sat down.

4
00:00:23.608 --> 00:00:30.526
"You must be a very forgiving person to visit after the way I've treated you," Mr. Pendleton said.

5
00:00:30.527 --> 00:00:34.316
"I apologize for my rudeness when you brought the beef stew.

6
00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:39.160
And I've never thanked you for helping me when I broke my leg. Thank you!"

7
00:00:39.161 --> 00:00:42.989
"I was glad to help you," Pollyanna said.

8
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:47.993
"I mean, I wasn't glad your leg was broken."

9
00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:52.978
"I understand what you meant." Mr. Pendleton smiled again.

10
00:00:52.979 --> 00:00:57.483
"You were brave that day in the woods, and the stew was delicious.

11
00:00:57.484 --> 00:01:01.510
Is there any more today that Aunt Polly didn't send?"

12
00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:08.817
Pollyanna's eyes widened at the reminder of Aunt Polly's scolding. "No, sir."

13
00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:12.792
Mr. Pendleton stared straight ahead, lost in thought.

14
00:01:12.793 --> 00:01:19.597
At last he sighed. "I didn't send for you to watch me mope.

15
00:01:19.598 --> 00:01:23.671
Go into the library—you know, the big room with the telephone.

16
00:01:23.672 --> 00:01:31.918
You'll find a wooden box in the cabinet with glass doors. Bring it here, please."

17
00:01:31.919 --> 00:01:36.356
A few minutes later, Pollyanna returned with the box.

18
00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:42.082
It was full of interesting things that Mr. Pendleton had picked up during his travels.

19
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:49.027
He had an entertaining story about every item, including an intricately carved chess set.

20
00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:54.881
They also talked about Pollyanna's life with Aunt Polly as well as her former home out West.

21
00:01:54.882 --> 00:01:59.903
Much too soon, it was time for Pollyanna to leave.

22
00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:03.627
"I want you to visit me often," Mr. Pendleton said.

23
00:02:03.628 --> 00:02:09.425
"I'm lonely, and there's another reason . . ." His voice trailed off.

24
00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:13.822
"When I first learned who you are, I didn't want to see you again.

25
00:02:13.823 --> 00:02:18.435
You reminded me of something I've tried to forget for years.

26
00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:23.049
But then the more I tried to forget, the more I remembered.

27
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.619
So now I want you to come. Will you?"

28
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.646
"Of course, Mr. Pendleton."

29
00:02:30.647 --> 00:02:35.993
Pollyanna's eyes were filled with sympathy for the sad-faced man.

30
00:02:35.994 --> 00:02:41.705
*** That evening after supper, Pollyanna sat in the backyard, talking with Nancy.

31
00:02:41.706 --> 00:02:48.116
"I can't believe Mr. Pendleton showed you all those things and told you stories about them."

32
00:02:48.117 --> 00:02:57.468
Nancy shook her head in amazement. "He's usually so grumpy—if he even bothers to speak."

33
00:02:57.469 --> 00:03:00.156
Pollyanna quickly defended her new friend.

34
00:03:00.157 --> 00:03:05.953
"People wouldn't think he's so bad if they knew him."

35
00:03:05.954 --> 00:03:12.979
Nancy swatted away a fly. "I don't understand why he's so interested in you.

36
00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.411
I mean, no offense, but he's not someone who likes children."

37
00:03:18.412 --> 00:03:22.461
Pollyanna smiled. "He didn't like me right away.

38
00:03:22.462 --> 00:03:27.502
Just today he admitted that, at first, he didn't want to see me again.

39
00:03:27.503 --> 00:03:31.804
I reminded him of something he wanted to forget and—"

40
00:03:31.805 --> 00:03:39.958
"Something he wanted to forget?" Nancy leaned forward with excitement. "What was it?"

41
00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:42.008
"He didn't say."

42
00:03:42.009 --> 00:03:46.016
"A mystery!" Nancy said in an awestruck voice.

43
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:49.616
"Just like in the mystery novels I love to read.

44
00:03:49.617 --> 00:03:57.215
Only this is a real-life mystery! Tell me every little detail."

45
00:03:57.216 --> 00:04:05.489
So Pollyanna told everything she could remember from the first time she met Mr. Pendleton until that day.

46
00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:11.766
"He didn't want to see you again after he learned you were Miss Polly's niece, right?" Nancy said.

47
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:15.080
"Yes, that's what he said today."

48
00:04:15.081 --> 00:04:20.749
"And he acted strange when you said Miss Polly didn't want him to think she'd sent the stew?"

49
00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.352
Nancy was growing more excited by the minute.

50
00:04:24.353 --> 00:04:26.766
"Yes, but—"

51
00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:32.864
"I've got it!" Nancy looked around to make sure nobody else was listening.

52
00:04:32.865 --> 00:04:36.614
"He and Miss Polly were sweethearts!"

53
00:04:36.615 --> 00:04:40.725
"What? Aunt Polly doesn't even like him.

54
00:04:40.726 --> 00:04:45.013
She didn't want him to think the beef stew came from her."

55
00:04:45.014 --> 00:04:49.230
"Tom told me that she had a sweetheart long ago.

56
00:04:49.231 --> 00:04:52.968
They had an argument and broke off their engagement.

57
00:04:52.969 --> 00:04:56.578
Tom said the man still lives in town!"

58
00:04:56.579 --> 00:05:00.482
Pollyanna still wasn't convinced, so Nancy pressed on.

59
00:05:00.483 --> 00:05:07.925
"Mr. Pendleton said you reminded him of someone. It has to be Miss Polly!"

60
00:05:07.926 --> 00:05:13.366
"But if they loved each other, they would have made up years ago."

61
00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:16.519
"Sometimes sweethearts can be stubborn."

62
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.470
Nancy had a dreamy look on her face.

63
00:05:20.471 --> 00:05:27.929
"Wouldn't it be wonderful if you taught them the Glad Game and they got back together?"

